{"id":"word:hebrew:H631","type":"word","title":"אָסַר","subtitle":"H631 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to yoke or hitch ; by analogy, to fasten in any sense, to join battle","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָסַר (H631) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 73 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָסַר (ʼâçar) means to yoke or hitch ; by analogy, to fasten in any sense, to join battle First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 18 44."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָסַר","transliteration":"ʼâçar","pronunciation":"aw-sar'","strong":"H631","lemmaId":"hebrew:H631","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["אָסְרָ֥ה","וַ/יֶּאְסֹ֖ר","וַ/יַּאַסְרֵ֨/הוּ֙","אָס֥וּר","אֲסוּרִ֥ים"],"morphs":[["HVqp3fs",9],["HC/Vqw3ms",6],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3ms",6],["HVqsmsa",5],["HVqsmpa",5],["HR/Vqc",4],["HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3ms",3],["HTd/Vqsmpa",3],["HVNi2ms",3],["HVqv2ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to yoke or hitch ; by analogy, to fasten in any sense, to join battle","usage":"bind, fast, gird, harness, hold, keep, make ready, order, prepare, prison(-er), put in bonds, set in array, tie.","full":"H631. asar [ אָסַר ] verb tie, bind, imprison (Arabic , Assyrian asâru , compare COT Gloss , Aramaic אֲסַר , , Ethiopic ) — Qal Perfect suffix אֲסָרָם Job 36:13 ; 3 feminine singular אָֽסְרָה Num 30:5 +, etc.; Imperfect יֶאְסֹר 1Kin 20:14 ; וַיֶּאֱסֹר Gen 42:24 ; וַיֶּאְסֹר 46:29 +; plural suffix יַאַסְרֻנִי Judg 16:7 etc.; Imperative אֱסֹר 1Kin 18:44 ; 2Kin 9:21 ; אִסְרוּ Jer 46:4 ; Psa 118:27 ; Infinitive absolute אָסֹר Judg 15:13 ; אָסוֺר 16:11 ; construct לָאְסֹר Num 30:3 +; לָאֱסוֺר Judg 15:10 ; לֶאֱסָרְךָ 15:12 ; אָסְרָם Hosea 10:10 ; Participle active construct אֹסְרִי Gen 49:11 ; passive אָסור 40:3 +; plural אֲסוּרִים 39:20 +; also Judg 16:21 , 25 Qr (Kt אסירים ); הָסוּרִים Eccl 4:14 (compare Now); אֲסֻרוֺת 2Sam 3:34 ; construct אסורי Gen 39:20 Kt (Qr אֲסִירֵי ); — 1 tie, bind , for security, foal to vine (followed by ל ) Gen 49:11 (blessing of Jacob); horses and asses 2Kin 7:10 (twice in verse); Psa 118:27 is dubious De bind the festal victim with cords ; Che bind the procession with branches , etc. 2 tie, harness , kine to ( ב ) cart 1Sam 6:7 , 10 ; so (metaphor) Hosea 10:10 harness them to ( ל ) their two iniquities (but Jerome Ew Now make ׳א here = יסר chastise , compare אֶסֳּרֵם v a ); also followed by accusative chariot Gen 46:29 (J) Exod 14:6 (E) 2Kin 9:21 ; absolute 1Kin 18:44 ; 2Kin 9:21 ; even of making ready chargers ׳א הַסּוּסִים Jer 46:4 (|| הַמָּרָשִׁים עֲלוּ ). 3 bind , with cords, fetters, etc., as prisoner, Simeon Gen 42:24 (E), Samson Judg 15:10 , 12 , 13 (3 t. in verse); 16:5 , 7 , 8 , 11 (twice in verse); 16:12 ; ׳א בַּנְחֻשְׁתַּיִם 2Kin 25:7 2Chr 36:6 = Jer 39:7 ; 52:11 ; also 2Chr 33:11 ; compare (without ׳בַּנ ) 2Kin 17:4 ( ׳א בֶּלָא בֵּית || עָצַת ), 23:33 ; compare of divine chastisement Job 36:13 & see also Ezek 3:25 ; Psa 149:8 ; figurative of absolute authority 105:22 ; especially Passive participle 2Sam 3:34 thy hands were not bound (|| and thy feet not put in fetters ); ׳א בָּאֿזִקִּים Jer 40:1 compare ׳א בַּזִּקִּים Job 36:8 (probably figurative || חַבְלֵיעֹֿ֑נִי ); metaphor of king held captive by a woman's tresses Cant 7:6; perhaps = imprisoned (whether bound or not) Gen 39:20 ; 40:3 , 5 (all J E); as substantive plural prisoners 39:20 (Kt, see above); so (late) as distressed, & object of divine compassion Isa 49:9 ; 61:1 ; Psa 146:7 ; האסי֯רים בֵּית prison Judg 16:21 , 25 ; compare Eccl 4:14 . 4 gird (rare & late) ׳א בְּמָתְנֵיהֶם אֵזוֺר Job 12:18 ( אֵזוֺר = slaves' waistcloth, RS p. 25 above; Hoffm reads וַיָּסַר for וַיֶּאְסֹר ); עַלמָֿתְנָיו אֲסוּרִים חַרְבּוֺ Neh 4:12 . 5 followed by מִלְחָמָה begin the battle, make the attack (compare German mit jemandem anbinden ) 1Kin 20:14 ; 2Chr 13:3 . 6 figurative of obligation of oath or vow (only Numbers 30, P) ׳א עַלנֶֿפֶשׁ , usually followed by accusative of congnate meaning with verb אִסָּר אֱסָר, Num 30:3 ; 30:5 (twice in verse); 30:6 ; 30:8 ; 30:9 ; 30:11 ; 30:12 ; without אֱסָר etc., 30:7 ; 30:10 ; compare 30:4 ׳א אִסָּר ( עַלנֶֿפֶשׁ omitted) Niph`al passive of Qal 3 , be, bound, imprisoned, Imperfect (jussive) יֵאָסֵר Gen 42:19 (E); 2 masculine singular תֵּאָסֵר Judg 16:6 , 10 , 13 (of Samson); Imperative הֵאָֽסְרוּ Gen 42:16 (E). Pu`al Perfect be taken prisoner אֻסְּרוּ Isa 22:3 ; אֻסָּ֑רוּ ib. אֵסוּר noun masculine Judg 15:14 band, bond (Aramaic אֱסוּר , ; on the form see Ges § 84a 12. R.) אֲסוּרָיו , of Samson 15:14 ; אֲסוּרִים Eccl 7:26 of hands of evil woman; הָאֵסוּר בֵּית = prison Jer 37:15 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 18 44","keyReferences":["1Kgs 18 44","1Kgs 20 14","1Sam 6 7","1Sam 6 10","2Chr 13 3","2Chr 33 11","2Chr 36 6","2Kgs 7 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":73,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 18 44","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":44,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֱסֹ֣ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqv2ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 14","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יֶאְסֹ֥ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 7","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/אֲסַרְתֶּ֤ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq2mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּאַסְר֖וּ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Chr 13 3","book":"2Chr","chapter":13,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יֶּאְסֹ֨ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"2Chr 33 11","book":"2Chr","chapter":33,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּֽאַסְרֻ֨/הוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"2Chr 36 6","book":"2Chr","chapter":36,"verse":6,"englishText":"","source